      "message": "Right — this file isn\u0027t imported as a normal module. \nThe issue is that multiprocessing re-executes the directly run main script during\nspawn/forkserver startup.\n\nFor a script path, CPython runs it again as `__mp_main__` via `runpy.run_path()`. Without the guard, that reaches `update_manpages.main()` again and tries to create another `Pool` while multiprocessing is still bootstrapping.\n\nThat\u0027s the failure I\u0027m fixing. I reproduced it on Linux with Python 3.14\u0027s default forkserver start method.\n\nThe test intentionally mirrors that `__mp_main__` path.\nI\u0027ll reword the commit/test text to say \"re-executes the main script\" instead of \"loads the module\".",
